In article <3219@ddsw1.MCS.COM> benfeen@ddsw1.UUCP (Ben Feen) writes:

>good thing is, if you start a game on a bones level, you will
>pick up some spellbooks. Just try to X some new spellbooks,
>and you might be "wrenched" away from those ghosts that invariably 
>build up on bones levells.

Spoiler below:



Bad thing, is spellbooks taken from ghosts are cursed. You might get
"wrenched" (i.e. randomly teleported) away from the ghost, because this
is a possible result of the curse. Most of the other results are much
less pleasant.

Even if you do get teleported away from him, there's still a ghost that's
after your hide, and you've wasted the spellbook.

You're better off getting rid of the ghost in the standard manner (described
here frequently) and then un-cursing all the spellbooks that you've found.

Suggestion for future versions: If a ghost kills you, it shouldn't still be
around in the bones file. Ghosts should be freed from this plane once they've
avenged themselves in some way. Future players would find the loot from the
first ghost (still cursed), plus the second ghost and all its loot. Of course,
if you were killed by something else, you'd still have multiple ghosts on
the level.
